WEBVTT

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:03.060
Riku has a fatal flaw.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.310
Nanase-san has a respiratory disorder.

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:08.230
You're not telling me to quit?

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:10.170
It can't function without you.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.570
The wind is blowing our way.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:13.950
Now's the time to act.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.200
The ticket site contacted us.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:17.830
They've sold out!

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.180
Riku-san.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.920
How are you feeling?

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.650
I'm taking my medicine.

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:35.760
I'm fine. I feel great.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.370
We have a run-through at 12.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:42.830
We'll only be confirming positions, 
so you don't need to go all out.

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:43.430
Got it.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:45.110
I won't push myself.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:47.900
When does the <i>LIVE X LIVE</i> broadcast start?

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:49.980
At 8:20 PM.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:52.820
It's a live show, so the 
time may be a little off.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:55.280
We'll be on a segment to
 present our concert to—

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.820
I wanna be on TV!

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.990
Then you'd better dance 
well so you'll stand out.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:04.160
Got it!

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:07.810
They'll be giving you instructions 
while you're onstage,

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:10.170
so make sure you adjust accordingly.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:14.840
Listening to instructions while 
performing is pretty hard.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.910
You'd better not miss any.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.560
Why are you telling me that?

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:20.890
Okay, okay. Don't waste your energy.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:22.960
That's all from me.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.720
Any questions?

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:28.310
My girl, only the most important question.

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:30.220
Are you happy?

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:33.690
Yes!

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:35.990
Great!

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:45.160
Gazing at the distant sky...

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:48.710
Someday we'll make it past there

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:54.310
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:01.140
We don't know what's right

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:04.350
So we Try and Jump!

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:07.520
Slamming face first into 
challenges and laughing

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:11.150
For us It's Only Way!

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:14.320
Make it shake (For Your Sky)

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:17.820
Make it reach (For Your Heart)

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:20.320
We'll change any and all kinds of pain

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:21.490
Do Live! (Yeah!)

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:22.320
Live! (Yeah!)

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:25.740
In the light!

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.540
(One, Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven Go!)

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:33.000
Yes Glory Days! Together 
we'll run through them

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.810
If your voice (Fuu!) reverberates (Dream!)

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:39.300
Then your wishes will become 
destiny (Singing New World!)

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:45.810
Give rise now to Age of Stage!

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:52.770
The future surely lies on the other side

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:55.690
Yes... It will keep on evolving

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:59.070
Our WiSH VOYAGE

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:05.330
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:13.960
Triumphant Return In The Rain

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:21.930
Okay, good.

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.050
Do you have any comments or questions?

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.310
We're good!

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:30.720
We'll do the same for the concert.

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:32.520
Thank you!

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:35.880
It looks like rain.

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:40.060
What's wrong?

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.410
We're singing here again.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:43.780
Yeah.

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:46.750
Only nine people came the first time.

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:48.410
But today it'll be a full house.

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:51.640
Our manager got this venue, 
and our fans are supporting us.

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:56.040
It makes me feel like I need to work harder.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:58.710
I want to answer their 
voices with all my might.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:02.470
Even if it means I collapse.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.060
Ow!

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.590
Don't you dare!

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:09.120
Just so you know, I'm mad about your illness.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:10.910
Sorry.

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:12.350
That's not what I meant.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:15.480
I'm telling you not to hide it
 like it's some bad thing.

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:19.560
There's nothing wrong 
with you or your illness.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:23.080
I can tell you're working hard.

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:26.570
But working hard and being reckless 
are two different things.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:31.080
We should careful so our fans can 
watch with carefree smiles.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:33.140
Yeah!

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:34.140
Riku-kun.

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:37.040
Want some warm tea?

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:39.240
Yes, please.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:41.590
It's easier to breathe when my chest is warm.

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:44.650
This is my favorite blanket.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:46.880
Careful you don't get cold.

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:47.640
Thanks.

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:51.520
Want some?

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:55.230
I'm okay. You guys worry too much.

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:56.770
Of course we do.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:05:00.470
You're the main vocalist of IDOLiSH7.

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:01.230
Iori.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:03.910
If you fall, we all go down with you.

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:06.530
We can't have you quitting or collapsing.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:08.600
You didn't need to put it like that.

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:09.450
Now I'm mad.

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:12.880
In any case, we're all worried about you.

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:13.880
You too, Yamato-san?

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:14.750
Huh?

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:18.580
I'm not good in serious situations.

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:19.890
How dishonest.

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:22.250
Look who's talking.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:26.540
If you can make it until the end,

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:29.340
I'll buy you a dirty mag from 
the convenience store as a reward.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:30.250
What?

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:33.260
Are you excited? You are around that age.

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:35.140
Yamato-san!

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:37.020
We're opening soon.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:39.610
Then let's pump ourselves up!

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:40.840
Yeah!

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:44.590
The end of the merchandise line is over here!

00:05:44.590 --> 00:05:47.990
Here's your T-shirt and towel.

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:50.570
Thanks for your support.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:05:59.830
<b>Greenroom</b>

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:03.340
We're back.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:04.990
Three thousand people...

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:09.050
Calm down. You'll be okay.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:10.700
We did practice a lot.

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:15.390
Yes. I even skipped three episodes 
of <i>MagiCona</i> to practice.

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:17.770
Let's do our best. A TV station's coming.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:19.820
You're all about that.

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:26.900
I'll sing so my voice reaches 
each and every person...

00:06:27.230 --> 00:06:28.750
alongside all of you!

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:33.700
What are you doing?

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:36.740
Join us. Come on, Manager.

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:38.160
Uh, but...

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:41.420
This way, please.

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:50.720
Back then and today, there's 
only one thing we can do.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:54.100
Let's give everything we've got.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:56.100
Okay, let's go!

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:57.760
Yeah!

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.420
Is it almost time?

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:14.530
Shaking your heart (Say!)

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:16.410
Shaking your beat (Shout!)

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:20.040
Racing through time

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:21.790
Jump! (High!) Jump! (High!)

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:29.010
This vivid GENERATiON with you

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:32.810
(One, Two, Three, Four, 
Five, Six, Seven, Jump!!!)

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:31.470
We are IDOLiSH7!

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.260
Let's have fun dancing today!

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:38.020
It's the beginning Don't look back

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:41.520
There's no time to look away

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.770
We found this Chance

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:48.440
We can't let it go

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:52.130
Once we start running it's Non stop!

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:55.030
Changing at dizzying speeds is our Vision

00:07:56.150 --> 00:08:01.240
Let's go find where the future

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:59.960
They're on fire...

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:05.800
That we wrote in that notebook is

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:07.710
Hello. We're with <i>LIVE X LIVE</i>.

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:11.820
We can start running at any time

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:10.090
We're ready to start filming.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:13.130
O-Okay, thank you.

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:13.130
(In this place that keeps changing)

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:18.640
Raise it up high, our Joker Flag

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:20.690
The wind's getting stronger.

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:21.910
We'll clash (and search)

00:08:20.690 --> 00:08:23.140
I wouldn't call this wind. 
And there's the rain, too.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.140
And someday turn into light

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:26.150
I hope they don't injure 
themselves, at least.

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:29.650
Excuse us.

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:31.850
The broadcast begins in five minutes.

00:08:31.850 --> 00:08:33.850
We're counting on all of you.

00:08:33.850 --> 00:08:34.910
Okay.

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:38.890
We'll be able to get some great shots.

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:40.410
Thank you.

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:53.010
Thanks, everyone!

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:55.920
This next song is our last song!

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:59.760
What?

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:07.310
Yes, Dancing BEAT!! Even farther away

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:10.610
Night and day!! I want to deliver

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:14.070
Never knowing what it means to stand still

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:21.120
Our future will be eternally Shooting!

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:31.420
La la la la... forever wish

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:37.590
La la la la...

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:43.220
When everything always goes your way

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:50.860
There's something important 
missing, right? A-ha!

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:57.360
So I'm proud of everything that made me cry

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:06.330
I'm prepared not to give 
up over the small things

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:14.810
Instead of staring at your 
feet, look into my eyes

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:22.400
Huh?

00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:23.260
What's going on?

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:33.830
I'm back.

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:34.520
What's the word?

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:37.150
No guests have reported any injuries.

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:39.570
IDOLiSH7 isn't experiencing 
any problems, either.

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:42.910
What about the lights and sound?

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:45.840
Both will take a little 
longer to come back online.

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:47.040
But...

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:50.140
We can't do the broadcast without sound.

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:53.520
We can power the overhead lights 
using the backup power supply.

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:55.850
There's no sound.

00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:58.520
Mine's silent, too. I can't hear anything.

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:00.630
What should we do? Should we keep going?

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:02.800
Wait. It's too dangerous to move around.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.210
We can't stop.

00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:05.180
Tamaki-kun?

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:08.820
Everyone who came today showed up 
even though they're busy, right?

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:11.520
They made time to come and see us.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:16.650
Yes. They're here seeking 
a dreamlike experience.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:23.120
If we can't make every 
moment the best possible,

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:25.720
there's no point in us 
standing onstage, right?

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:29.160
We're professionals, too. Let's do it.

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:33.950
Stop the cameras. Cancel the broadcast.

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:35.500
Please keep broadcasting.

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:36.040
Huh?

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:38.680
Shine the lights on the stage.

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:39.470
Huh?

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:40.570
Okay.

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:48.350
<i>Even if the sound can't reach 
them, their dancing will!</i>

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:53.850
So bright...

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.780
Guys, clap your hands!

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:03.360
Hey, everybody! Hands up!

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:05.000
Huh?

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:06.620
Clap, clap!

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:27.250
We have spare parts. We can—

00:12:27.250 --> 00:12:28.360
Well?

00:12:28.360 --> 00:12:29.750
Still nothing.

00:12:29.750 --> 00:12:30.720
I'll go check it out.

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:32.500
Yes. Yes, got it.

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:34.140
We have sound!

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:37.230
Sogo-san!

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:39.980
Roger that.

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:46.240
<i>We're turning on the sound in five.</i>

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:09.600
Good job, Tamaki-kun.

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:12.100
It's all you, So-chan.

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:20.650
When I look to my sides 
I see my friends there

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:31.870
And you're smiling there 
in front of me... Be there!

00:13:32.190 --> 00:13:33.870
Right? Dancing DREAM!!

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:36.540
Even farther away...

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:40.800
Yes, Dancing BEAT!! Even farther away

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:44.170
Night and day!! I want to deliver

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:50.800
Never knowing what it means to 
stand still keep charging ahead

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:52.560
That performance...

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:54.490
Right? Dancing BEAT!! An even more wonderful

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:53.810
Was so cool!

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:55.680
Sogo-san!

00:13:54.490 --> 00:13:57.560
Night and day!! Thrill

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:57.560
IDOLiSH7 is the best!

00:13:57.560 --> 00:14:01.350
We'll search for it together

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:01.570
Looks like we'll be able to finish.

00:14:01.350 --> 00:14:05.550
Our future will be eternally Shining!

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:04.070
There's gonna be a huge reaction to this.

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:23.090
Our future will be eternally Shining!

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:28.930
We are the eternal Dreamer!!

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:35.890
La la la la... forever wish

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:42.120
La la la la...

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:13.050
What did you want to discuss?

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:16.290
It's about that idol group 
that's popular right now.

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:19.070
I heard you got into a fight with them.

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:21.400
You mean IDOLiSH7?

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:22.480
That's right.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:27.080
They pose no threat to you, but 
they'll make good materials.

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:32.350
We'll emphasize and spread 
the story that they tried to

00:15:32.350 --> 00:15:34.460
steal guests from your concert.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:40.800
By creating a sense of enmity, your fans 
will become even more devoted to you.

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:43.280
A sense of enmity, huh?

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:46.250
That's a great third-rate idea.

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:49.490
Is this how Yaotome 
Productions does business?

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:51.330
Tenn, don't speak to the president that—

00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:53.390
It's fine. Keep going.

00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:58.590
Do you call making your fans anxious 
and unhappy doing business?

00:15:59.340 --> 00:16:02.350
Isn't that what an 
attention-hungry child does?

00:16:03.740 --> 00:16:06.520
You're as vitriolic as ever, Tenn.

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:09.760
Enthusiasm, attachment, devotion.

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:14.200
Controlling the hearts of 
people is our business.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:18.160
All you need to do is follow 
the path I've drawn for you.

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:21.880
The path of glory leading to the top.

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:25.250
Control, huh?

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:28.640
Don't think you can control 
everything with your remote.

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:33.050
Let's go, Tenn, Ryu.

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:35.520
Excuse us.

00:16:35.520 --> 00:16:37.800
Sorry. Excuse us.

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:42.380
You can't control me.

00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:48.280
So impudent.

00:16:48.280 --> 00:16:50.480
Just like his mother.

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:54.440
IDOLiSH7...

00:16:54.950 --> 00:17:00.950
There are plenty of ways to destroy 
a brand new and unstable group.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:03.870
Prepare yourself, Takanashi.

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:10.390
<i>Yes Dancing BEAT!! Even farther away</i>

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:13.630
<i>Night and day!! I want to deliver</i>

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:15.070
We're so small, and the clip's so short.

00:17:13.630 --> 00:17:15.070
<i>Never knowing what it means—</i>

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:18.890
You can't tell who we are.

00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:25.500
Uh, um, I...

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:26.590
I'm a fan!

00:17:26.590 --> 00:17:28.600
I saw your live broadcast!

00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:29.860
Thank you.

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:32.110
Osaka-san, please shake my hand!

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:32.700
Huh?

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:35.160
Hey, I heard Osaka Sogo's over there!

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:36.280
What?

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:38.990
Thank you.

00:17:41.420 --> 00:17:43.280
Tamaki-san, look this way!

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:45.250
I'm eating ice cream right now.

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:46.460
Your dancing was amazing!

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:47.870
Can I have your autograph?

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:49.790
He's so hot up close!

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:51.250
I should've gotten a T-shirt!

00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:55.380
I said, I'm eating ice cream right now!

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:57.380
He's so cute!

00:17:57.380 --> 00:17:59.100
That's amazing.

00:17:59.100 --> 00:18:01.550
You guys are both really popular.

00:18:02.030 --> 00:18:05.950
We just happened to be 
on during the broadcast.

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:08.480
Don't be modest. You were both cool.

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:12.500
Tama, what did you think 
of your first time on TV?

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:14.250
You wanted to be on TV, right?

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:16.490
That wasn't good enough.

00:18:18.010 --> 00:18:19.160
Excuse me.

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:21.890
Sogo-san, Tamaki-san.

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:23.240
Do you have a minute?

00:18:23.710 --> 00:18:25.250
A request for a TV appearance?

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:29.370
Yes. It's a late-night show, 
but it's on a national network.

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:30.580
When?

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:33.090
We haven't accepted yet.

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:37.070
And it's a request primarily for you two.

00:18:37.070 --> 00:18:38.190
Us?

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:41.300
Yes. We received a pre-show survey.

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:44.130
What do you do on your days off?

00:18:44.130 --> 00:18:46.180
What do you like about each other?

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:48.430
What was your first 
impression of each other?

00:18:52.430 --> 00:18:55.150
We don't talk when we're together, though.

00:18:56.590 --> 00:18:59.120
It's probably the effects 
of the live broadcast,

00:18:59.120 --> 00:19:02.200
but we've received a lot 
of other jobs for you two.

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:04.910
Being on a national
 network is a big chance,

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:08.200
but IDOLiSH7 is a seven man group.

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:10.830
I thought I'd get your opinions first.

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:12.420
Sorry, but I don't—

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:13.150
I'll do it.

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:13.880
Tamaki-kun?

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:15.950
We're gonna be on national TV, right?

00:19:15.950 --> 00:19:17.050
You have to accept!

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:19.290
We operate as seven.

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:21.640
We can't have them treating us like a duo.

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:22.720
I don't care.

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:23.930
Well, I do.

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:26.340
I don't want to betray our friends.

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:28.310
We wouldn't be betraying them!

00:19:27.370 --> 00:19:28.310
Um...

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:30.190
In any case, I'm doing it.

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:33.120
If you don't like it, you can stand 
next to me with your mouth shut.

00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:34.980
Listen, Tamaki-kun.

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:38.270
You don't have to sing. 
I'll do it all myself.

00:19:38.270 --> 00:19:40.330
So accept the job.

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:41.910
I can't handle you.

00:19:44.970 --> 00:19:46.080
Hey.

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:46.080
Sogo-san.

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:47.490
Wait!

00:19:48.510 --> 00:19:50.240
I told you to wait!

00:19:50.240 --> 00:19:52.460
Why don't you go cool your head?

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:52.960
Sogo-san and Tamaki?

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:55.120
Why?

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:57.590
Our manager said this is 
a big chance for us, too!

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:59.180
There's no point if it's just us!

00:19:59.180 --> 00:20:00.470
Why don't you get that?!

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:02.560
Tamaki-san, Sogo-san!

00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:03.950
This is unexpected.

00:20:03.950 --> 00:20:07.660
I wasn't expecting our group's first 
fistfight to be between these two.

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:09.470
Is this the time to be easygoing?

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:11.180
Guys, calm down.

00:20:11.180 --> 00:20:12.840
Take your hands off him.

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:14.600
You're scaring the manager.

00:20:18.800 --> 00:20:19.860
What happened?

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:22.620
It's nothing.

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:24.500
I just spoke out of turn.

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:26.400
What? Why hide it?

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:27.320
Tell them!

00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:28.660
It's not something we should say.

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:30.770
You called them your friends!

00:20:30.770 --> 00:20:33.180
There are some things you don't 
need to tell your friends!

00:20:33.180 --> 00:20:35.740
Guys, cool down.

00:20:35.740 --> 00:20:37.380
Are you hiding something?

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:42.300
So-chan and I got an offer to appear on TV.

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:44.570
Just the two of you?

00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:46.830
You guys are happy for us, right?

00:20:46.830 --> 00:20:47.630
Right?

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:57.050
Wait!

00:21:00.600 --> 00:21:02.990
Why didn't you discuss this with me?

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:05.440
Since you're a member,

00:21:05.440 --> 00:21:10.060
I thought you'd feel conflicted about 
something relating to your popularity...

00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:11.920
You say that now?

00:21:12.560 --> 00:21:14.400
Let me guess my rank.

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:16.870
I'm probably fourth from the top.

00:21:17.820 --> 00:21:19.250
You're right.

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:21.890
Whether you accept or turn down this offer,

00:21:21.890 --> 00:21:26.860
unless management determines our 
direction, you'll only cause strife.

00:21:28.910 --> 00:21:31.350
I wouldn't feel that way.

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:35.350
Even if I were told afterwards, 
I would wish I'd been consulted.

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:40.480
The manager values our opinion and theirs.

00:21:41.770 --> 00:21:44.740
But they're completely 
split on their opinions.

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:49.740
Why did you want to become an idol?

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:49.100
Why is Tamaki so obsessed with TV?

00:21:51.180 --> 00:21:53.240
So-chan, wait!

00:21:53.240 --> 00:21:55.210
Listen to me!

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:57.520
Repeat yourself all you
 want, I won't accept.

00:21:57.520 --> 00:22:00.000
Well, I'm not giving up, either.

00:22:04.430 --> 00:22:08.400
You're IDOLiSH7's Osaka Sogo 
and Yotsuba Tamaki, aren't you?

00:22:08.940 --> 00:22:11.160
Who's this old dude?

00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:14.640
Surely you recognize the president 
of Yaotome Productions.

00:22:15.060 --> 00:22:16.190
TRIGGER's?

00:22:17.520 --> 00:22:19.850
Come with me for a bit, will you?

00:22:34.300 --> 00:22:37.840
Start running (beyond)

00:22:37.840 --> 00:22:44.850
Your imagination... Alive

00:22:53.010 --> 00:22:58.410
If you desire something from 
the bottom of your heart

00:22:58.410 --> 00:23:03.230
Risk your life and dive in

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.320
The resolve to discard what's truly important

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:13.450
Is the boat that will take you to new sights

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:15.990
(Hey man!) Take the strings of your heart

00:23:15.990 --> 00:23:18.540
(Hey man!) And stretch them

00:23:18.540 --> 00:23:21.420
(Say dream!) To the limit

00:23:21.420 --> 00:23:26.340
At the other end you're sure 
to find the Gate to paradise

00:23:26.760 --> 00:23:32.340
You'll be the first witness

00:23:32.340 --> 00:23:37.130
Our pounding pulses are Heavenly

00:23:37.130 --> 00:23:42.150
Admit that you can't deny it

00:23:42.460 --> 00:23:46.610
We start... What do your fingertips

00:23:46.610 --> 00:23:51.080
Seek now?
